

**8. Legendre Functions**

**Mathematical Properties**

**Notation**

The conventions used are \(z{=}x{+}iy\), \(x\), \(y\) real, and in particular, \(x\) always means a real number in the interval \(-1{\leq}r{\leq}+1\) with cos \(\theta{=}x\) where \(\theta\) is likewise a real number; \(n\) and \(m\) are positive integers or zero; \(v\) and \(\mu\) are unrestricted except where otherwise indicated.

Other notations are :

\[P^{n}(x)\text{ for }\frac{n!P_{n}(x)}{(2n{-}1)!!}\]

\[P_{nn}(x)\text{ for }(-1)^{n}P_{n}^{m}(x)\]

\[T_{n}^{n}(x)\text{ for }(-1)^{n}P_{n}^{m}(x)\]

\[\overline{P_{n}^{m}}(x)\text{ for }(-1)^{n}\sqrt{\frac{(2n{+}1)(n{-}m)!}{2(n{+} m)!}}P_{n}^{m}(x)\]

\[\Phi\sharp(z)\text{ for }P_{\sharp}^{n}(z)\text{, }\mathbb{C}_{\sharp}^{n}(z)\text{ for }Q_{\sharp}^{n}(z)\]

\[\mathbb{C}_{\sharp}^{n}(z)\text{ for }e^{\omega z!}Q_{\sharp}^{n}(z)\]

\[Q_{\sharp}^{n}(z)\text{ for }\frac{\sin\left(\psi+u\right)\pi}{\sin\,\nu\pi}\,Q_{\sharp}^{n}(z)\]

Various other definitions of the functions occur as well as mixing of definitions.

**8.1.3**

\[Q\sharp(z){=}\,e^{i\omega x^{2}-\nu-1/2!}\,\frac{\Gamma(\nu{+}{\pm}{+}1)}{ \Gamma(\nu{+}{\pm}3)}\,z^{-\nu-\mu-1}(z^{2}{-}1)^{\flat\mu}\,F\left(1{+}{\frac{ \nu}{2}}{+}{\frac{\mu}{2}},{\frac{1}{2}}{+}{\frac{\nu}{2}}{+}{\frac{\mu}{2}}; \,{\frac{1}{2}}{+}{\frac{\mu}{2}};\,{\frac{\nu}{2}}{+}{\frac{3}{2}};{\frac{1}{2}} \right)\quad(|z|{>}1)\]

**Alternate Forms**

(Additional forms may be obtained by means of the transformation formulas of the hypergeometric function, see [8.1].)

